    "guilt"
  ],
  "verse_ref": "Romans 8:1",
  "verse_text": "There is therefore now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus.",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "Romans 8:1",
      "text": "There is therefore now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus."
    },
    {
      "ref": "2 Corinthians 7:10",
      "text": "Godly sorrow produces repentance leading to salvation without regret…."
    },
    {
      "ref": "John 14:6",
      "text": "I am the way, and the truth, and the life…."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "core_idea",
      "label": "Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Many men believe every uncomfortable feeling comes from God.",
            "It doesn’t."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Some discomfort is conviction.",
            "Other discomfort is condemnation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "One draws you toward God.",
            "The other pushes you away from Him.",
            "One produces repentance.",
            "The other produces shame.",
            "One says, “Come home.”",
            "The other says, “Stay away.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Learning the difference changes everything."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "read_this_out_loud",
      "label": "Read This Out Loud",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "The enemy wants you focused on your failure.",
            "God wants you focused on His grace.",
            "One keeps you stuck.",
            "The other sets you free."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "moment_after_the_failure",
      "label": "Moment After the Failure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Most men know what it feels like to fail.",
            "To say the wrong thing.",
            "To lose their temper.",
            "To fall back into old patterns.",
            "To drift."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "The question is: what voice speaks next?"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Failure is often followed by a conversation.",
            "Not with another person.",
            "With yourself.",
            "And what you hear next matters."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "two_different_voices",
      "label": "Two Different Voices",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Conviction says: “What you did was wrong.”",
            "Condemnation says: “You are what’s wrong.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Conviction addresses behavior.",
            "Condemnation attacks identity.",
            "Conviction is specific.",
            "Condemnation is vague and overwhelming.",
            "Conviction leads to repentance.",
            "Condemnation leads to hiding."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "romans_8_1",
      "label": "Romans 8:1",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Paul makes an astonishing declaration: there is now no condemnation.",
            "Not less condemnation.",
            "Not reduced condemnation.",
            "No condemnation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Why?",
            "Because Christ already carried the judgment.",
            "The enemy wants you to keep carrying what Jesus already carried."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "godly_sorrow_and_worldly_sorrow",
      "label": "Godly Sorrow and Worldly Sorrow",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Godly sorrow says, “I need God.”",
            "Worldly sorrow says, “I’m hopeless.”",
            "Godly sorrow moves toward restoration.",
            "Worldly sorrow moves toward despair."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_part_most_men_miss",
      "label": "The Part Most Men Miss",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus tells the truth.",
            "To Peter. To the woman at the well. To Zacchaeus. To the disciples.",
            "He never minimizes sin.",
            "But He also never weaponizes truth."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus reveals truth for redemption.",
            "Not humiliation.",
            "The goal of conviction is not punishment.",
            "The goal is restoration."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "root_check",
      "label": "Root Check",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Surface thought: “I failed again.”",
            "Possible root: shame, self-condemnation, perfectionism, fear of rejection.",
            "Deeper question: What voice am I agreeing with?",
            "Core lie: “My failure defines me.”",
            "Truth: My failure may explain my struggle. It does not define my identity."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "gem_to_carry",
      "label": "Gem to Carry",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Conviction says, “This behavior must die.”",
            "Condemnation says, “You should.”",
            "Only one of those sounds like Jesus."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "prayer",
      "label": "Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus,",
            "Thank You that You tell the truth without rejecting me.",
            "Thank You that You convict without condemning.",
            "Help me recognize the difference between Your voice and the voice of accusation.",
            "Teach me to repent quickly.",
            "Teach me to receive grace deeply.",
            "Break every agreement I’ve made with shame.",
            "Remind me that my identity is found in You, not my failures.",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
